% The query of exists-streamed.dl, a check after the literal that binds its
% key, answered with every answer gathered first.  a has two edges, so a
% lookup in the check's place would derive a twice; the check derives it
% once, and gathering it in the answer relation gives the same rows as
% streaming it.  The counters show the answer relation holding both.

edge(a, b).
edge(a, c).
edge(b, c).
node(a).
node(b).
node(e).

node(X), edge(X, _)?
